# Docker build context exclusions (Plan III §8.4).
# The builder stage COPYs only the workspace manifests, packages/, apps/,
# and src/ — everything below is secret, generated, or local state that
# must never enter the build context (and therefore never the image).

# VCS metadata and local secrets / runtime state
.git
.secrets
.vow
.vow-cache
.argo_overrides

# Dependencies and build outputs (rebuilt inside the image)
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/dist
apps/githubio/out
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Local env files. Runtime configuration is bind-mounted by
# docker-compose at run time, never baked into the image. The tracked
# templates under src/ (default.env, example.env, example.env.enabler)
# do NOT match these patterns — their names do not start with ".env" —
# and stay in the context on purpose: the orchestrator reads them at
# runtime and locates the workspace root via src/default.env.
**/.env
**/.env.*

# Coverage artifacts
**/coverage
